'' A METHOD NAMED LIKE A STATEMENT KEYWORD, called from a sibling: own or inherited, with or
'' without parentheses, as a statement or for a value. fbc looks the name up before it tries
'' the statement, so it is the method -- measured on fbc-modern 1.20, this program prints the
'' four lines below. 'Close( )' over an inherited method stopped on TKO0994, 'Get( )' and
'' 'Name( )' were refused as bad statements, and 'r = Close( )' silently became fb_FileCloseAll.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/mir/src/method-named-like-statement-run.bas -o tests/mir/methodnamedlikestatementrun.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/mir/methodnamedlikestatementrun.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  11101113
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  112
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  42 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: plain
cleanup
